{"exhaustive":{"nbHits":false,"typo":false},"exhaustiveNbHits":false,"exhaustiveTypo":false,"hits":[{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"QECTOR"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"partial","matchedWords":["v3","multi"],"value":"Qector-Decoder-<em>v3</em>: <em>Multi</em>-Back End Software Architecture for QEC"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://zenodo.org/records/21850315"}},"_tags":["story","author_QECTOR","story_49221031"],"author":"QECTOR","created_at":"2026-08-08T12:05:07Z","created_at_i":1786190707,"num_comments":0,"objectID":"49221031","points":2,"story_id":49221031,"title":"Qector-Decoder-v3: Multi-Back End Software Architecture for QEC","updated_at":"2026-08-08T12:19:00Z","url":"https://zenodo.org/records/21850315"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"aurelianware"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"partial","matchedWords":["v3","multi"],"value":"Hi HN,<p>I'm launching Cloud Health Office <em>v3</em>.0.0 \u2014 an open-source platform for healthcare payer EDI integration.<p>## The Problem<p>Healthcare payers (insurance companies) spend 6-8 weeks integrating each new payer for EDI transactions (claims, eligibility, prior auth). The process is:\n- Entirely manual\n- Vendor lock-in heavy\n- Compliance-intensive (HIPAA, CMS regulations)\n- Expensive ($50k-$100k per integration)<p>With the CMS-0057-F deadline (Jan 1, 2027), most payers need to support FHIR APIs but have no clear path.<p>## What I Built<p>A production-ready platform that:\n- Handles X12 EDI (270/271/276/277/278/837/835/275) \u2194 FHIR R4 transformation\n- Deploys to any cloud (Azure/AWS/GCP via Kubernetes)\n- Zero-code payer onboarding (5 minutes vs weeks)\n- CMS-0057-F compliant out of the box\n- 424 automated tests<p>Tech stack: TypeScript/Node.js, Kubernetes, Argo Workflows, Kafka, HashiCorp Vault<p>## Why Open Source<p>Healthcare interoperability should be a solved problem. The industry is fragmented with proprietary solutions. I wanted to create a reference implementation that:\n- Shows how to do FHIR properly\n- Avoids vendor lock-in\n- Reduces barrier to entry for health tech startups\n- Helps payers meet regulatory deadlines<p>## Current Status<p>- <em>v3</em>.0.0 just shipped (<em>multi</em>-cloud support)\n- 424 tests passing\n- Production deployments in test environments\n- Apache 2.0 license<p>Repo: <a href=\"https://github.com/aurelianware/cloudhealthoffice\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/aurelianware/cloudhealthoffice</a><p>Would love feedback from the HN community, especially around:\n- <em>Multi</em>-cloud deployment patterns\n- FHIR implementation edge cases\n- Healthcare compliance automation<p>Happy to answer questions!"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"partial","matchedWords":["multi"],"value":"Show HN: Cloud Health Office \u2013 Open-source <em>multi</em>-cloud EDI+FHIR platform"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://github.com/aurelianware/cloudhealthoffice"}},"_tags":["story","author_aurelianware","story_46883119","show_hn"],"author":"aurelianware","created_at":"2026-02-04T08:32:18Z","created_at_i":1770193938,"num_comments":0,"objectID":"46883119","points":1,"story_id":46883119,"story_text":"Hi HN,<p>I&#x27;m launching Cloud Health Office v3.0.0 \u2014 an open-source platform for healthcare payer EDI integration.<p>## The Problem<p>Healthcare payers (insurance companies) spend 6-8 weeks integrating each new payer for EDI transactions (claims, eligibility, prior auth). The process is:\n- Entirely manual\n- Vendor lock-in heavy\n- Compliance-intensive (HIPAA, CMS regulations)\n- Expensive ($50k-$100k per integration)<p>With the CMS-0057-F deadline (Jan 1, 2027), most payers need to support FHIR APIs but have no clear path.<p>## What I Built<p>A production-ready platform that:\n- Handles X12 EDI (270&#x2F;271&#x2F;276&#x2F;277&#x2F;278&#x2F;837&#x2F;835&#x2F;275) \u2194 FHIR R4 transformation\n- Deploys to any cloud (Azure&#x2F;AWS&#x2F;GCP via Kubernetes)\n- Zero-code payer onboarding (5 minutes vs weeks)\n- CMS-0057-F compliant out of the box\n- 424 automated tests<p>Tech stack: TypeScript&#x2F;Node.js, Kubernetes, Argo Workflows, Kafka, HashiCorp Vault<p>## Why Open Source<p>Healthcare interoperability should be a solved problem. The industry is fragmented with proprietary solutions. I wanted to create a reference implementation that:\n- Shows how to do FHIR properly\n- Avoids vendor lock-in\n- Reduces barrier to entry for health tech startups\n- Helps payers meet regulatory deadlines<p>## Current Status<p>- v3.0.0 just shipped (multi-cloud support)\n- 424 tests passing\n- Production deployments in test environments\n- Apache 2.0 license<p>Repo: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;aurelianware&#x2F;cloudhealthoffice\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;aurelianware&#x2F;cloudhealthoffice</a><p>Would love feedback from the HN community, especially around:\n- Multi-cloud deployment patterns\n- FHIR implementation edge cases\n- Healthcare compliance automation<p>Happy to answer questions!","title":"Show HN: Cloud Health Office \u2013 Open-source multi-cloud EDI+FHIR platform","updated_at":"2026-03-05T23:31:09Z","url":"https://github.com/aurelianware/cloudhealthoffice"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"pretext"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"partial","matchedWords":["v3"],"value":"<a href=\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.2\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-<em>V3</em>.2</a><p><a href=\"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news251201\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news251201</a>"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"partial","matchedWords":["v3"],"value":"DeepSeek-<em>v3</em>.2: Pushing the frontier of open large language models [pdf]"},"url":{"fu